4.13 Conclusion
The Climate-Smart Improved Kienyeji Chicken Broiler Production Enterprise successfully demonstrated that poultry farming is a viable and sustainable enterprise for St. Mary's Girls Secondary School – Thigio. Through proper planning, effective management, and adoption of climate-smart practices, the Form Four Agriculture candidates successfully reared 60 improved Kienyeji chicks, with 51 birds surviving to the marketing stage.
The project enhanced practical agricultural skills, promoted entrepreneurship, strengthened environmental stewardship, and demonstrated the importance of integrating modern livestock production techniques with sustainable resource management. The experience gained will continue to benefit future Agriculture candidates and contribute to the school's practical agriculture programme.
